<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haigerloch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haigerloch is a small town on the Eyach in the Zollernalb district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The lordship of Haigerloch passed to the counts of Zollern in 1497 in exchange for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhazuns">Rhäzüns</a> and was the seat of a separate line of counts after the division of 1576. In 1945 a cellar beneath its castle church housed the last German experimental nuclear reactor, captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/haigerloch.jpg" alt="Haigerloch" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roman Eisele · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haigerloch_-_Altstadt_-_Ansicht_aus_S%C3%BCden_vom_R%C3%B6merturm_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
